{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1140120-aeon-trinity-campaign-fell-apart","id":1140120,"title":"Aeon Trinity Campaign Fell Apart","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum","Trinity Continuum: \u00c6on"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-09-14T02:36:10-07:00","id":1140120,"title":"Aeon Trinity Campaign Fell Apart","content":"I ran a campaign in the Aeon Trinity space opera universe. I spent a lot of time, invested money getting out of print source material, then people lost interest, went down to 2 core members, then they lost interest too before I could have a nice end to the campaign. Why did it fall apart? My lack of experience made the fights last too long and seem boring. I should have set stricter limits on power and behavior. Also, in the course of play, one of my players, a friend I have know for about a year, who was based in the Federated State Military, revealed himself to be sympathetic to the fascist government that ruled what use to be the United States because it fit the ideology he concealed from me.I improvised a new plot for the campaign, even though I felt a bit horrified to play with him. What is the right thing to do? Perhaps I could start another campaign with different players in the future with the lesson I have learned.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8102-doctor-zero","name":"Doctor Zero","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-14T06:06:31-07:00","id":1140142,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Doctor Zero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1140120-aeon-trinity-campaign-fell-apart#post1140120\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Perhaps I could start another campaign with different players in the future with the lesson I have learned.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds like the best option. Good luck having a better campaign in future. I hope it works out for you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-16T16:08:19-07:00","id":1140919,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1140120-aeon-trinity-campaign-fell-apart?p=1140142#post1140142\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sounds like the best option. Good luck having a better campaign in future. I hope it works out for you.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Agree completely with Bunyip here. I've GM'd many Aeon (Trinity) games since it came out including both home-brew and the published scenarios. They've all gone very well, and am presently GMing the Darkness Revealed books for like the 5th time, but for a bunch of Aeon newbies. Its about finding the right group, setting expectations in advance.... and possibly getting a better handle on the rules to speed up play. Combat, for example, can work fairly quickly with just a little bit of practice. Good luck!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#ff0000\"><b>Ad Astra</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/232-chill","name":"CHILL","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar232_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-16T16:25:04-07:00","id":1140921,"title":"","content":"Sorry to hear that. The FSA Setting is rather harsh and one should come at it with a lighter touch. Not to mention creepily prescient as this was written before the decidedly Crony Capitalist environment we find ourselves in now. I tend to think when running in the setting much like operating in the former Soviet block of the Cold war era (I grew up at that time) and apply the kinda of lessons and paranoia needed to portray it as such. Totalitarianism, no matter the source, pretty much acts the same. And most people on the ground are not going to care overly much about the particulars of ideology other than they want it to stop. Or support, if they get something out of it. For handling FSA adventures for characters, Good old cloak and dagger paranoia is the order of the day. and subtle attempts at ideological subversion will be needed to make any progress against it that means something. for players, make them work hard for the small victories. with the way things are set up, they will need to take solace in those.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13091-thewanderingjewels","name":"TheWanderingJewels","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13091_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-18T00:57:37-07:00","id":1141340,"title":"","content":"Hey Doc Zero.<br /> <br /> Okay there are different issues at hand:<br /> Players: You don\u00b4t need to play with people with whom you are uncomfortably with. What I noted from your games that your players ist, that they quit the game without talking with you what bothered them about the game. I can only recommend that - in the future - you do after the first game a feedback sessions, where everyone can adress what they liked and disliked about the game. So everyone can adapt and find solutions to problems at hand. i.e. your players don\u00b4t like hours of crunchy fighting scene. Cut them short! Handle a fight between 2 parties just with 1-3 dice rolls and resolve it via storytelling. Also ask everyone what they expect from the game and tell them what you do!<br /> Did the player or the portrayed character showing himself to the Trinity FSA Military government?<br /> <br /> tl;dr: Open communication FTW!<br /> <br /> The FSA -<br /> The Military rules everything. Most people live of foodstamps, meanwhile there is no normal police force anymore and policemen act more like soldiers.<br /> Cities are divided by sectors and only people directly working for the military or allied companies have relative freedom of movement and business. Barter economy is rapamt in the arcologies.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Gamelines: Requiem, Lost, Awakening, Trinity Continuum: Aeon, some V5.<br /> Likes cheesecake (quark-based)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1305-maekkel","name":"maekkel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1305_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"206"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-04T23:08:01-08:00","id":1165243,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Doctor Zero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1140120-aeon-trinity-campaign-fell-apart#post1140120\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I ran a campaign in the Aeon Trinity space opera universe. I spent a lot of time, invested money getting out of print source material, then people lost interest, went down to 2 core members, then they lost interest too before I could have a nice end to the campaign. Why did it fall apart? My lack of experience made the fights last too long and seem boring. I should have set stricter limits on power and behavior. Also, in the course of play, one of my players, a friend I have know for about a year, who was based in the Federated State Military, revealed himself to be sympathetic to the fascist government that ruled what use to be the United States because it fit the ideology he concealed from me.I improvised a new plot for the campaign, even though I felt a bit horrified to play with him. What is the right thing to do? Perhaps I could start another campaign with different players in the future with the lesson I have learned.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Here's some GMing basics I've learned over 29 years of RPG. Take them for what they're worth.<br /> <br /> In your specific case, players must not conceal backgrounds. If the player is too embarrassed to tell you the truth about his character at the start, then that's a red flag to the player and about the player. You have a person you cannot trust around other human beings. It's one thing for you and a player to work out some secret you both agree to keep from the players until the time is right to spring the plot twist upon them, but a player doesn't get to take that decision upon himself.<br /> <br /> More generally in terms of combat, what I did with this game was during a combat round, each player had to give me a brief explanation of what they were going to do before we executed the round. &quot;Fire my gun&quot;, &quot;Use pyrokinesis&quot;, &quot;run and dive over those crates, and roll back to my feet and shoot 3 people&quot;. This allowed me to make sure they were clear on what they were telling me they were doing. It allowed me to say things like &quot;that's 6 separate actions, you'll be out of dice after 4&quot;, or &quot;you realize the room is filled with explosive gas and any use of pyrokinesis means certain death for everyone, right?&quot;<br /> <br /> It committed each player to their actions, and then we rolled. Then....I walked back through with a description of what just happened. Blow-by-blow I explained it and added some cinematic detail. It really helped change the combat from a slog into a mad sequence of action-packed events.<br /> <br /> Oh, and I also employed a technique whereby any player who dilly-dallied or changed his mind more than once &quot;lost his action to indecision&quot;. Also, anyone who wanted to take the time to assess the scene also lost any actions other than counting the number of enemies still standing, or figuring out where all the moving pieces were, etc. No one got to hog time by cheating their way through the night for an unfair advantage. Either pay attention and keep up, or take the time to reassess what's going on, but you don't get to be a douche in my games.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23574,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23574-arch-stanton","user":"Arch Stanton","date":". 12-05-2017, 02:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23574-arch-stanton","name":"Arch Stanton","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}